('APX-S-4839-1', 'APX-C-4839', 1, null, null, null, 'Create an ultra-realistic cinematic video of an airplane flying steadily through the sky that transforms mid-flight into a modern rocket and rapidly ascends toward the upper atmosphere. The sequence should begin with the airplane in stable forward motion under natural lighting, maintaining realistic scale, perspective, and aerodynamics.', null, null, 'The sequence should begin with the airplane in stable forward motion under natural lighting, maintaining scale, perspective, and aerodynamics.', null, null, null, null, null, null),
('APX-S-4839-2', 'APX-C-4839', 2, null, null, null, null, 340, 402, 'During the transformation, the airplane must reconfigure through visible mechanical movement: wings retract and fold inward, engines compress and merge into a central propulsion system, and the fuselage reshapes into a sleek cylindrical…', null, 'sliding', null, null, null, null),
('APX-S-4839-3', 'APX-C-4839', 3, null, null, null, 'Avoid smooth morphing — the transformation must feel engineered and physically plausible. Once the rocket form is complete, the engine ignites with an intense, bright exhaust plume featuring a white-hot core and glowing edges. Add strong heat distortion and air turbulence behind the thrust.', null, null, 'Avoid smooth morphing — the transformation must feel engineered and physically plausible. Once the rocket form is complete, the engine ignites with an intense, bright exhaust plume featuring a white-hot core and glowing edges.', null, null, null, null, null, 'intense'),
('APX-S-4839-4', 'APX-C-4839', 4, null, null, null, 'The rocket then sharply pitches upward and accelerates rapidly toward the upper atmosphere, leaving a long, powerful exhaust trail. Motion should follow realistic physics with increasing speed, visible acceleration, and dynamic motion blur. The sky should subtly transition from lower atmosphere tones to deeper blue as altitude increases.', null, null, 'The rocket then sharply pitches upward and accelerates rapidly toward the upper atmosphere, leaving a long, powerful exhaust trail. Motion should follow physics with increasing speed, visible acceleration, and dynamic.', null, null, null, null, null, null),
